	description: "A person is also a capacitor if you think about it",
	text: [
		"First capacitor, discharges as much as you'd want it to for the early game.",
		"",
		"You may configure the capacitor to charge, equal, or discharge it's power, open the Battery Socket's GUI, at the right-most side you will see two battery icons with arrows, these change how the capacitor interacts with the power grid.",
		"",
		"- Green configuration \"equal\", shares power to the grid and maintains excess power.",
		"- Orange \"discharge\", discharges all of the capacitor's power into the grid.",
		"- Blue \"store\", stores all of the power the battery receives.",
		"",
		"These two buttons have specific conditions, for when the Battery Socket is not powered by redstone and when it's powered.",
		"",
		"You may also change the priority of the specific Battery Socket, a higher priority does it's configured behaviour much faster."
